# Per-engagement TARGET SCOPE for black-box LIVE testing (target-gateway).
#
# This file is the single source of truth for what the pentest agents are
# allowed to touch over the network during a black-box live engagement. It is
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT: if a host is not listed here, every request to it is dropped
# at target-gateway, no matter which tool or agent asked. The agents CANNOT
# widen this scope; only the human operator edits it, and it is mounted
# read-only into target-gateway.
#
# Copy the authorized targets out of the signed requirement spec / rules of
# engagement into this file, then arm the engagement with:
#
#   ./scripts/pentest-task.sh --mode blackbox --live \
#       --scope-file config/engagement-scope.conf   "<task...>"
#
# (The launcher stages this file into engagement/scope/ where target-gateway
# reads it. See docs/blackbox-live-testing.md.)
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT  (same as config/allowlist.conf):
#   host[:port]            exact host, optionally pinned to a port
#   *.suffix[:port]        wildcard: the apex and any subdomain of suffix
#   # comment              a full-line comment
#
# Optional per-host RATE directive (honor a spec-stated request-rate limit so
# the target is not slowed or blocked). Put it as a trailing comment:
#   api.example.com:443   # rate: 3     -> cap this host at 3 req/s
# When a host has no "# rate:" directive the gateway falls back to
# TARGET_RATE_DEFAULT (.env). Either way the cap is multiplied by
# TARGET_RATE_SAFETY_FACTOR to stay comfortably under the stated limit, and the
# gateway backs off further if the target returns 429/503/Retry-After.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nothing is in scope by default. Uncomment / add ONLY the hosts the spec
# authorizes. Examples (replace with the real authorized targets):

# A single authorized web application, spec says "max 3 requests/second":
# app.example-target.com:443    # rate: 3

# Its API host, no stated limit -> uses TARGET_RATE_DEFAULT:
# api.example-target.com:443

# An authorized staging subdomain tree (apex + all subdomains):
# *.staging.example-target.com:443

# IMPORTANT
# - Do NOT add third-party / shared-infrastructure hosts (CDNs, analytics,
#   login providers) unless the spec explicitly authorizes them. Out-of-scope
#   egress (including any tool trying to "phone home") is dropped here by
#   design, which is exactly what keeps testing inside the sandbox.
# - Prefer HTTPS targets (:443). Weak target TLS is reported as a finding, not
#   a reason to disable verification elsewhere.
